result.summary:
Rung L is approved with no fix. The code generator now compiles a block's local functions. Each one becomes a closure class built the way forFnExpr builds one for a function expression. A function reaches itself as the closure's own this, and reaches its siblings through fields that are set once, after the whole group exists and before the block's body runs. A local function's name, whether called or passed as a value, goes through its closure, recognised by its unambiguous name. These forms are still refused, each with its own error message: static parameters of its own, two local functions of one name in a block, the atomic modifier, a contract, and varargs.

Test first holds in the worker's transcript. The five run tests failed on the base's code ('Tests run: 10,  Failures: 10') before the edit was first built, and passed in the final run after the last code change ('OK (53 tests)').

I ran three programs of my own on both paths, old code against new, at 1 and 4 threads (SkLoop, SkEdge and SkShadow under /home/user/fortress-codegen-local-functions/tmp/rung-codegen-local-functions/skeptic/). They cover:
- parallel loops with atomic updates;
- a block run again on each pass of a while loop;
- a local function returning a function expression that calls its sibling;
- recursion that crosses nested blocks;
- two blocks of one function declaring the same name;
- generic and size-generic contexts;
- object field initialisers and getters;
- self and siblings passed as values;
- a top-level variable's initialiser.

Every value matched walk on both the new and the old code; the old compiled path stops at 'Can't compile LetFn'.

The worker's code-generator measure is confirmed from its files. It ran on dbf4825e0's code and shows 38 refused declarations in 10 kinds. The LetFn kind is gone and all nine library declarations emit.

No stage was owed: the only changed path outside the free list is CodeGen.java, which neither stage reaches. The report's citations, its sentences made false and its ledger homes check out. REPORT.md and record.md were already on the branch, so the journal step wrote nothing and took no commit. SKEPTIC.md is committed at /home/user/fortress-codegen-local-functions/explorations/compile-ladder/rung-codegen-local-functions/SKEPTIC.md and pushed.
